---
import Slide from "@/components/slides/Slide.astro";
import Code from "@/components/slides/Code.astro";
import Table from "@/components/slides/Table.astro";

const notes =
    'Run the query live against the frozen demo.\n\n- the question is always: who waits, and who holds?\n- 812 (the worker) is active, waiting on a lock. "transactionid" means it\'s waiting for another transaction to finish\n- blocked_by points to 804: ours, "idle in transaction", a transaction open and doing nothing\n- the database is telling us the culprit is doing nothing. doing nothing is the bug\n- every major database has this view (footnote: mysql, sql server)';
---

<Slide
    kicker="scenario 1 · the autopsy"
    title="step 1: ask the database who's waiting."
    notes={notes}
>
    <Code
        lines={[
            "select pid, application_name, state, wait_event,",
            "       pg_blocking_pids(pid) as blocked_by",
            "from pg_stat_activity;",
        ]}
    />
    <Table
        code
        head={["pid", "application_name", "state", "wait_event", "blocked_by"]}
        rows={[
            ["812", "receipt-worker", "active", "transactionid", "{804}"],
            ["804", "orders-api", "idle in transaction", "—", "{}"],
        ]}
        highlight={1}
    />
    <p class="s-big">
        the lock holder is us, and it's idle.{" "}
        <span class="s-accent">doing nothing is the bug.</span>
    </p>
    <p class="s-small mt-auto">
        illustrative output · mysql: sys.innodb_lock_waits · sql server:
        blocking_session_id in sys.dm_exec_requests
    </p>
</Slide>
